        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Updated scrollbar styling example with new colors that have sufficient contrast.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">An A11Y team was looking at this page:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Scrollbars_styling\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Scrollbars_styling</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">and noted the red on yellow isn't meeting 1.4.11 contrast requirements of 3 to 1.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">They suggested color combo that work (that are interesting):</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Teal<br>\nthumb #0B4F4A<br>\ntrack #5F9E98<br>\nbackground #FFFFFF</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Purple<br>\nthumb #4B0082<br>\ntrack #9E7FD0<br>\nbackground #FFFFFF</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46113",
            "title": "Revise scrollbar colors in CSS guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-12T14:34:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-12T14:31:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143878990?u=a497d43bf9f6bbe6c308a73145be33c540facb48&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fix the <code class=\"notranslate\">GainNode</code> constructor options in the Advanced Web Audio API guide to use <code class=\"notranslate\">gain: 1</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">value: 1</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In the Web Audio API specification, the <code class=\"notranslate\">GainOptions</code> dictionary accepts <code class=\"notranslate\">gain</code> (float), not <code class=\"notranslate\">value</code>. Passing <code class=\"notranslate\">value: 1</code> has no effect because <code class=\"notranslate\">value</code> is not a member of <code class=\"notranslate\">GainOptions</code>. Using <code class=\"notranslate\">gain: 1</code> correctly initializes the gain audio parameter matching the W3C specification and MDN's <code class=\"notranslate\">GainNode()</code> constructor reference.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Reference: <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/webaudio/#GainNode\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web Audio API Specification - GainOptions</a></li>\n<li>Reference: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GainNode/GainNode\" rel=\"nofollow\">MDN GainNode() constructor reference</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #46078.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5781287902\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46078\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/46078/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46078\">#46078</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46112",
            "title": "Fix GainNode constructor options in advanced Web Audio guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-12T13:21:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-12T13:20:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rajpreetcodes",
                "url": "https://github.com/rajpreetcodes"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Documented the new <code class=\"notranslate\">Sanitizer.setJavascriptURLs()</code> method</li>\n<li>Documented the <code class=\"notranslate\">javascriptURLs</code> option of <code class=\"notranslate\">SanitizerConfig</code>, with its defaults for the constructor, the safe methods and the unsafe methods</li>\n<li>Updated <code class=\"notranslate\">Sanitizer.removeUnsafe()</code>: it now also sets <code class=\"notranslate\">javascriptURLs</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code></li>\n<li>Listed the removal of <code class=\"notranslate\">javascript:</code> URLs in the XSS-safe baseline and the default sanitizer configuration, which didn't mention it before</li>\n<li>Added a \"JavaScript URLs\" section to the usage guide</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Working on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617219222\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45898\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45898/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45898\">#45898</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2068934\" rel=\"nofollow\">Firefox bug 2068934</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5334784953\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12898\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/12898/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12898\">whatwg/html#12898</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-is