        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2891702?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add reference pages for <code class=\"notranslate\">BluetoothRemoteGATTServer.maxWriteWithoutResponseSize</code> and its <code class=\"notranslate\">maxwritewithoutresponsesizechanged</code> event, including an example of chunking write-without-response data. Link both from the interface page.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Status</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Draft until <a href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672/hovercard\">the specification change</a> and <a href=\"https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7879985\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chromium implementation</a> land, and browser-compat-data has entries for the new property and event. The new pages link to the proposal directly and do not show compatibility tables yet.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">ChromeStatus: <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5177569273053184\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5177569273053184</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46081",
            "title": "Document Web Bluetooth maximum write-without-response size",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T21:19:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T21:17:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hjanuschka",
                "url": "https://github.com/hjanuschka"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75755802?u=232cfdb37381645af6e176bf8b8b2a4d1d3a3495&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a paragraph to \"Focusable elements should have interactive semantics\" on the Keyboard accessible guide: in browse mode, some screen readers intercept <kbd>Enter</kbd> and <kbd>Space</kbd> and activate the element with a <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code> event, so <code class=\"notranslate\">keydown</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">keyup</code> handlers never run. Touch screen readers fire <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code> on double tap. The paragraph tells readers to handle <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code> as well, or use a native <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code>. Also adds the <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code> event to the section's \"See also\" list and fixes \"event handlers keyboard events\" to \"event handlers for keyboard events\".</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The section only recommends keyboard event handlers. A custom control built that way does nothing for an NVDA user in browse mode, which is the case reported in the issue.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>NVDA discussion of the behavior: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"286453272\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvaccess/nvda/issues/7898\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvaccess/nvda/issues/7898/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvaccess/nvda/issues/7898\">nvaccess/nvda#7898</a></li>\n<li>Checked in Chromium: a focused <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code> fires <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code> on both Enter and Space; a focused <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;div tabindex=\"0\"&gt;</code> gets only <code class=\"notranslate\">keydown</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">keyup</code>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">markdownlint-cli2</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">prettier -c</code> pass on the file.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #37887.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2821371672\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37887\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37887/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37887\">#37887</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46079",
            "title": "Keyboard accessible: note that screen readers can replace key events with click",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T17:09:53.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T17:08:19.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jsabutis",
                "url": "https://github.com/jsabutis"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome added support for the CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">ruby-overhang</code> property in version 151; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6560118298771456\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6560118298771456</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">ruby-overhang</code> page to the modern state of the property, including covering the <code class=\"notranslate\">spaces</code> value.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">cc'ing <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/jja08111/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/jja08111\">@jja08111</a>. Can I get a technical review of this PR, please?</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46076",
            "title": "Update ruby-overhang page to latest state, with spaces value",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-12T14:48:11.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T13:56:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">From version 149, Chrome adds the ability for features of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Payment_Request_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Payment Request API</a>/ <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web-Based_Payment_Handler_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web-based Payment Handler API</a> to reject with an <code class=\"notranslate\">OperationError</code> to specifically indicate an internal error coming from the payment handler app, as opposed to user cancellation. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5942637229113344\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5942637229113344</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is now true of the <code class=\"notranslate\">PaymentRequest.show()</code> method and the <code class=\"notranslate\">PaymentRequestEvent.respondWith()</code> method.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds information about <code class=\"notranslate\">OperationError</code> to each method's page and does a bit of cleanup.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
